Root cause:
The bug was caused by objtool's inability to correctly detect gcov support in older versions of GCC, which do not generate symbols with the 'gcov.' prefix. This led to unnecessary 'unreachable instruction' warnings being reported even when gcov was enabled, particularly in GCC version 4.6.4. The fix involved moving the gcov check out of objtool and introducing a new '--no-unreachable' flag to suppress these warnings when gcov is enabled, ensuring compatibility with older GCC versions.
